# audit-public.patterns.example — copy to tools/audit-public.patterns and fill it in.
#
# The copy is gitignored, and it has to be: a list of what must not be published is itself the
# thing that must not be published. tools/audit-public.sh reads it, or the file AUDIT_PATTERNS
# names, and adds these classes to its built-in ones.
#
#   id ~ bulk ~ ERE, matched case-insensitively ~ what it is
#
# Tilde-separated, because every useful regex here holds `|`. `bulk` is `yes` for a class that
# is counted rather than listed. One class per line; `#` lines and blank lines are skipped.
#
# A LITERAL LIST IS AS COMPLETE AS ITS LAST EDITOR. Write each name the way the repository
# writes it — a board named in prose with a space is a branch name with a hyphen — and give a
# class its reason, or nobody can review it.

client~no~northwind~the client's parent company
product~no~zephyr~the client's product
employer~no~initech~an employer named in the record
person~no~\b(morgan|altuser)\b~a person other than the user
client-hw~no~\b(acme|xr-100|widget[ _-]board|widget-pinout)\b~a real client's hardware
